                        ],
                        "form": "ка́пельны"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b83a166e-e569-3645-8743-8346084798ac",
                        "entry_id": "bd8e6664-685a-335f-bd63-ec4f44a824de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным капля"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f9e0cca-64b9-4f46-8401-9c64062b07b2",
                                "sense_id": "b83a166e-e569-3645-8743-8346084798ac",
                                "text": "Хлорацетон прибавлялся по каплям из капельной воронки."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ddcbd28-f89f-3711-8dc6-888932721498",
                        "entry_id": "bd8e6664-685a-335f-bd63-ec4f44a824de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "такой, как у капли"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ccb4215-cecf-4e9d-ad5d-41ced73640cc",
                                "sense_id": "3ddcbd28-f89f-3711-8dc6-888932721498",
                                "text": "Их своеобразную капельную форму со свойственными всем метеоритам углублениями нетрудно воспроизвести, если продувать горячую струю пара через кусок сургуча."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "324ccdf2-4661-353c-8d4c-2420bc546d1d",
                        "entry_id": "bd8e6664-685a-335f-bd63-ec4f44a824de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг. самый малый, крохотный, крошечный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "721da871-3601-4dc3-9f86-ac70b5d0e3c1",
                                "sense_id": "324ccdf2-4661-353c-8d4c-2420bc546d1d",
                                "text": "Замети ли ― целое облако белых кружев и крошечная, капельная туфелька с французским каблучком…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47b88604-eebb-4d2a-b618-aad00f029cd4",
                                "sense_id": "324ccdf2-4661-353c-8d4c-2420bc546d1d",
                                "text": "И ещё так, что забудет что-нибудь, то вспоминает, вспоминает ― и всё, всё до капельной капельки, до синь-пороха ему рассказала."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c47868e-5d84-481d-b354-4d717ef23ad1",
                                "sense_id": "324ccdf2-4661-353c-8d4c-2420bc546d1d",
                                "text": "― Там я хоть в самой малой, капельной мере, но способствую делу освобождения, прости за высокий стиль, а здесь я иждивенец войны…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a592146b-5155-49e4-ae8d-e0edbfaad200",
                        "source_entry_id": "bd8e6664-685a-335f-bd63-ec4f44a824de",
                        "target_lang_word": "drip",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "drip",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "622a6ac4-f132-3b30-b177-a26094cf5fcb",
                                        "entry_id": "f3ee4eb8-cf63-3c32-947f-75be835ca30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fall one drop at a time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25675a9f-ca1f-470b-b852-406ab7f9a179",
                                                "sense_id": "622a6ac4-f132-3b30-b177-a26094cf5fcb",
                                                "text": "Listening to the tap next door drip all night drove me mad!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "030a7e63-858b-3570-ac28-6a6b7f677a37",
                                        "entry_id": "f3ee4eb8-cf63-3c32-947f-75be835ca30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To leak slowly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51c14e72-0ea1-445a-a5d8-651e379f9e20",
                                                "sense_id": "030a7e63-858b-3570-ac28-6a6b7f677a37",
                                                "text": "Does the sink drip, or have I just spilt water over the floor?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "363ad1f6-44f7-311c-b167-ef77e89113b3",
                                        "entry_id": "f3ee4eb8-cf63-3c32-947f-75be835ca30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To let fall in drops."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dff73f2c-4a35-48f6-a576-52e6e61ace67",
                                                "sense_id": "363ad1f6-44f7-311c-b167-ef77e89113b3",
                                                "text": "After putting oil on the side of the salad, the chef should drip a little vinegar in the oil."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "801b71f4-80d6-4a58-9524-0bc00387a8de",
                                                "sense_id": "363ad1f6-44f7-311c-b167-ef77e89113b3",
                                                "text": "My broken pen dripped ink onto the table."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39c3af2a-45e0-4f38-ad3f-905f5caf9bc6",
                                                "sense_id": "363ad1f6-44f7-311c-b167-ef77e89113b3",
                                                "text": "c. 1726, Alexander Pope (probable author), The Lamentation of Glumdalclitch\nWhich from the thatch drips fast a shower of rain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31d3a00f-d529-4bb2-a40c-97e7ac9858f7",
                                                "sense_id": "363ad1f6-44f7-311c-b167-ef77e89113b3",
                                                "text": "Philander went into the next room[…]and came back with a salt mackerel that dripped brine like a rainstorm. Then he put the coffee pot on the stove and rummaged out a loaf of dry bread and some hardtack."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd592233-77a0-37e1-848a-b3192501ca07",
                                        "entry_id": "f3ee4eb8-cf63-3c32-947f-75be835ca30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To have a superabundance of (something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c57cc44b-3c4a-4e3b-a4b8-5797b46905ee",
                                                "sense_id": "dd592233-77a0-37e1-848a-b3192501ca07",
                                                "text": "The Old Hall simply drips with masterpieces of the Flemish painters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a50013de-76ba-487e-9458-5d1cd43363fc",
                                                "sense_id": "dd592233-77a0-37e1-848a-b3192501ca07",
                                                "text": "The duchess was dripping with jewels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8220eaa9-0179-3236-b3bb-1e475e913209",
                                        "entry_id": "f3ee4eb8-cf63-3c32-947f-75be835ca30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To rain lightly; to drizzle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07d47f99-ba36-4304-acc6-b72abf6cacb3",
                                                "sense_id": "8220eaa9-0179-3236-b3bb-1e475e913209",
                                                "text": "The weather isn't so bad. I mean, it's dripping, but you're not going to get so wet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a9c108f-ebf1-3d0b-bb4e-c2a19e2aa636",
                                        "entry_id": "f3ee4eb8-cf63-3c32-947f-75be835ca30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be wet, to be soaked."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "26e7d236-cb3a-35f0-8dca-29ca5fe895c8",
                                        "entry_id": "f3ee4eb8-cf63-3c32-947f-75be835ca30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To whine or complain consistently; to grumble."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e474b7a1-ede3-42e6-b437-9f64a9456194",
                                                "sense_id": "26e7d236-cb3a-35f0-8dca-29ca5fe895c8",
                                                "text": "The Women's Royal Naval Service was integrated with the Royal Navy in November 1993. […] Men interviewed by Public Eye (April, 1994) said they should 'stop dripping about it' and that women should learn to 'take it like a man […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dabac53-0323-41bf-9e18-4748033eb747",
                                                "sense_id": "26e7d236-cb3a-35f0-8dca-29ca5fe895c8",
                                                "text": "The government had been slowly running down the Royal Navy Organisation to save money on various peoples' budgets, so now we had to sub-contract ships to go to war! So stop dripping and \"make it so\", all those admirals can't be wrong!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6de77da7-4d18-359c-b1ea-c6dda4e15af2",
                                        "entry_id": "f3ee4eb8-cf63-3c32-947f-75be835ca30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Be impressive or attractive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "stative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd24fd39-1573-427b-ad0a-acb76143345b",
                                                "sense_id": "6de77da7-4d18-359c-b1ea-c6dda4e15af2",
                                                "text": "I'm sorry for drippin', but drip is what I do. And one of these days, I'm gon' get dressed and drip all over you."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "drip",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
